ACTION AND COORDINATES
Each column reconstructs one parity-compatible real Fourier coefficient,
applies the validated D13 signed real one-step map, projects back to the same
Fourier block, and stores one reduced column. The action includes framework
periodic exchange, project radial ghost fill, direct target-d=4 RHS, live
gauge, fixed lapse source, sigma=0.3 KO, outer valid-surface override, locked
four-stage RK, and cleanup. The field-scaled matrix is D^-1 M D, so it is a
similarity transform and has the same eigenvalues as the physical-coordinate
matrix. LAPACK's packed right and left eigenvectors transform as
v=D v_s and w=D^-1 w_s. The reported physical-coordinate
eigenvalue-conditioning proxy is ||w|| ||v|| / |w_s^dagger v_s|; it is not
labeled a formal condition number.

