The deterministic formula mutation gives physical proxy 19.1401 and old
scaled-coordinate proxy 5.79318, a 69.7% difference, and is rejected.
Across the actual spectra the maximum old/corrected difference is 849% and
879%. The identity w^dagger v=w_s^dagger v_s and a second deterministic
diagonal-similarity transformation pass for every real and packed-complex
eigenvector. Direct diagonalization of the unscaled matrix validates both
transformed leading left and right eigenvectors.

Six representative columns per sector, twelve total, are checked at both
epsilon values. All matrix entries are finite. The fixture emits all 576
complex eigenvalues and Omega=log(lambda)/dt values for each sector.
The conservative resolved-rate gate is |Re(Omega)| >= 2e-4, based on the
dense/direct action discrepancy divided by dt. Near-neutral signs below this
gate remain reported but are not classified as growth or decay. Eigenvalues
whose magnitude is not at least ten direct residuals also cannot pass.

