The resolved positive k=pi/4 spectral leader is an inner-boundary/constraint
mode. The k=pi/2 spectral leader is unresolved-near-neutral and constraint
heavy, with nearby rates clustered. The corrected relevant-mode proxies do
not establish severe leader nonorthogonality, so conditioning alone no
longer explains D13's local alignments. The supported interpretation is
limited to boundary/constraint spectral-radius rejection plus an unresolved
clustered block. No candidate passes the preliminary physical filter.
Both per-mode summaries report severe_leader_nonnormality=false. The
aggregate interpretation now uses those leader tests; spectrum-wide large
proxies are reported separately and are not promoted into a D13 explanation.

